% categories are POSIX: the byte 0xE9 is a letter and 0xB5 is a letter here, as the C library says, and the locale
% is not UTF-8.  The string-flag probes use it as the non-UTF-8 locale whose character classes differ from C.
LC_IDENTIFICATION
title      "Latin-1 ctype test locale"
source     ""
address    ""
contact    ""
email      ""
tel        ""
fax        ""
